# Citation metadata in the Citation File Format (https://citation-file-format.github.io),
# read by GitHub for "Cite this repository". Keep `version` equal to the version in
# Project.toml and CITATION.bib (checked in test/runtests.jl), and update `date-released`
# with each release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "PlanetTools.jl"
abstract: >-
  Julia package with tools for post-processing and analyzing output of climate model
  simulations for Earth and other planets, developed with focus on NASA GISS's ModelE and
  ROCKE-3D: NetCDF input and output, derived variables, area-weighted and temporal
  statistics, trends and their significance, ensemble statistics, aerosol and dust size
  distributions, and plotting of fields with missing data.
